Package: oneqrelay
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: oneq <k@1q.ro>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.13), python3 (<< 3.14), libssl3t64 (>= 3.5), adduser, util-linux
Suggests: nginx, supervisor
Section: net
Priority: optional
Description: federated registry and relay for the oneq post-quantum layer-2 mesh
 oneqrelay is the rendezvous server of a virtual Ethernet network.
 It keeps communities, user accounts (scrypt password hashes), registered
 nodes and their automatically allocated IP and MAC addresses, relays
 datagrams between nodes that cannot reach each other directly, and
 replicates all of this to other oneqrelay servers (federation).
 .
 It never sees traffic in clear: nodes talk end to end with a hybrid
 X25519 + ML-KEM-768 handshake. The HTTPS API speaks TLS 1.3 with
 X25519MLKEM768 only (via a dedicated OpenSSL configuration or a reverse
 proxy with the same restriction).
 .
 Installed in /opt/oneq/relay, configured by /etc/oneq/relay.conf. Runs under systemd or supervisord. Needs Python 3.13 linked against OpenSSL 3.5 or newer (Debian 13). The
 Python libraries it uses are bundled in /opt/oneq/relay/site-packages.
 This is an educational project without an independent security audit.
